=== section pi_instance ===
{
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "description": "Declaration-order pi graph-node ID. This is the only ID namespace allowed at route/order/sharing endpoints.",
      "pattern": "^i[0-9]+$",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "mechanism": {
      "description": "Pi mechanism is one closed source-neutral event class. realize is a generic representation-only stage when no more specific class applies. One realize instance anchored directly to a J.signature handle or C slot may be discharged by that parameter binding and its direct routed use; it does not require an identity assignment. Multiple instances anchored to the same handle still denote distinct routed use-sites/stages. address_base is an independently compiler-visible, program-uniform pointer/base stage before lane broadcast or lane-varying addressing; Lift uses it only when that separate source stage exists. address_lane is the compiler-visible stage that forms lane-varying final addresses. When routes contain address_base -> address_lane, Replay must materialize two distinct stages in that order and must not algebraically fold them into one flat vector offset. transfer_direct and transfer_async classify data movement after address formation; update_atomic and update_privatized classify physical update realization; synchronize classifies synchronization. Region placement='program' only scopes an instance to one program; it does not assert that a program/grid coordinate is read. A compiler-visible program/grid coordinate is a separate realization stage and requires its own realize instance and routes. Its source-neutral encoding is a realize instance anchored to the corresponding J domain in a program region whose scalar dependency path enters address_base before transfer; a domain/C dependency path entering address_lane is lane-varying instead. Replay must preserve this base-versus-lane distinction and U_f maps it to public frontend APIs. Integer coordinate arithmetic is a realize stage, not address_base or address_lane merely because the resulting integer is later used as a pointer offset. If source forms one complete base-plus-lane integer coordinate and then performs one pointer addition, Lift records that single pointer operation as address_lane; it must not invent an extra pointer address_base for the coordinate's program-uniform component. Replay must not invent program_id, a grid offset, or an affine address stage from region placement, grid convention, or C alone. Address classes never carry an index/offset formula, constant, integer width, cast, dtype, shape, vector length, predicate, fill, frontend API, or logical access semantics.",
      "enum": [
        "realize",
        "address_base",
        "address_lane",
        "transfer_direct",
        "transfer_async",
        "update_atomic",
        "update_privatized",
        "synchronize"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "region": {
      "pattern": "^r[0-9]+$",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "semantic_ref": {
      "description": "Anchor into a declared anonymous J/C handle. It is not a pi graph-node ID and never appears directly at route/order/sharing endpoints.",
      "pattern": "^(t|n|a|d|e|q|b|s|v|p|c|x)[0-9]+$",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id",
    "semantic_ref",
    "region",
    "mechanism"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}

